<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! face.draft.proposes ~ a seat proposes one batch; the operator's hand lifts

`proposals` lists {title, revision, text | digest, taint}: the daemon title and revision the item distils, its body (or the body's sha-256 digest) and every input from outside the face (a web page, tool output, pasted text); an AI summary inherits the taint of what it summarised. ONE batch per call rides the face's intents plane, pinned to this device; it carries digests and never a body, and it GRANTS NOTHING: the operator's hand lifts it with `lares kahua lift <title> proposal=<id>`.

TWO DIGESTS, ONE WORD. A proposal's `digest` names the BODY digest, the sha-256 of the raw body bytes (UTF-8, lowercase hex); the seat's tool computes it from `text`. The ROW digest that `kahua stage` prints and `lift --digest` takes covers the body AND the row's carried fields, so it differs. Hand `text`, or the BODY digest; a proposal built from the ROW digest refuses at the lift with `proposal-digest`, as does one whose body differs by a byte from the staged row's.

Any seat proposes. The seat's tool rides a local `seat` session over the @daemon wire, whose profile the vessel refuses every kahua pin, lift, withdraw and carry; no tool lifts (`face.draft.stages` writes the local row a lift names). Returns {id, cid}.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ a-batch · on-a-named-face

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-batch` params=`proposals/<proposals> ~ one proposal batch: a list of {title, revision, text or digest, taint}`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`on-a-named-face` params=`proposals/<proposals> face/1 ~ propose on one face inside the lent set`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ proposals · face · session

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`proposals` params=`takes/json-list needs/required ~ the batch: a list of {title, revision, text | digest, taint}, never empty (a JSON list on the terminal)`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/handle-index ~ any face inside the lent set, by persona index (a whole number from 0); absent, the worn face; a face outside the set refuses 'face-not-lent', a shut one 'face-not-open'`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`session` params=`takes/session-id skins/mcp ~ the seat session the call rides; absent, the tool's own`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ seat-or-hand

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`seat-or-hand` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ a proposal grants nothing: the operator's signed lift decides; it rides the face's intents plane pinned to this device, and a seat session proposes as the hand does`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ kahua-proposal-proposals · proposals-malformed · face-not-lent · face-not-open · proposal-digest

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`kahua-proposal-proposals` params=`cure/[[face.draft.proposes proposals/<proposals>]] ~ name proposals as a non-empty list of {title, revision, text | digest, taint}`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`proposals-malformed` params=`cure/[[face.draft.proposes proposals/<proposals>]] ~ --proposals needs JSON`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`face-not-lent` params=`~ the face stands outside the lent set the seat may name`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`face-not-open` params=`~ the face stands shut; open it first`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`proposal-digest` params=`~ at the lift: a proposal built from the row digest, or whose body differs by a byte from the staged row's, refuses there`>>
```

